{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 12,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.049,
            0.432,
            0.067
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "？ What are the maximum possible marks in the exam? What are the minimum possible marks?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.142,
            0.847,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 2:** There is an elevator in a mining shaft that moves above and below the ground. The elevator’s positions above the ground are represented as positive integers and positions below the ground are represented as negative integers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.231,
            0.471,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "(a) The elevator moves 3 metres per minute. If it descends into the shaft from the ground level (0), what will be its position after one hour?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.35,
            0.471,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "(b) If it begins to descend from 15 m above the ground, what will be its position after 45 minutes?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.433,
            0.252,
            0.452
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.457,
            0.471,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "Solution to part (a) of the question:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.485,
            0.215,
            0.843,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.506,
            0.26,
            0.524
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Method 1:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.526,
            0.471,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "We can model this using subtraction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.564,
            0.847,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "The elevator moves at 3 metres per minute. So in one hour it moves 180 metres (60 × 3). If it started at ground level (0 metres) and descended, we should subtract 180 from 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.418,
            0.632,
            0.578,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "0 = 180 = (-180).",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.66,
            0.846,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": "So, it will reach the (–180) metre position, which is 180 metres below the ground."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.705,
            0.26,
            0.723
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Method 2:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.724,
            0.847,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "Let us say that the speed and direction of the elevator are represented by an integer (metres per minute). It is +3 when it is moving up and it is (–3) when moving down."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.781,
            0.846,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "Since the elevator is moving down, the speed is (–3) metres per minute. It moves for 60 minutes. So it goes"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.83,
            0.584,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": "6 0 \\times ( - 3 ) = ( - 1 8 0 ) .",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": "36"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
